# `module::Model::make`

[Back to `module::Model`](../Model.md)

Builds a model of a given kind from a plain list of numbers, validating it.

## Signature

```cpp
static module::Model module::Model::make(model::Kind kind, std::span<const double> params, pluss::Config cfg = f64_default());
static module::Model module::Model::make(model::Kind kind, std::initializer_list<double> params, pluss::Config cfg = f64_default());
```

## What It Does

Creates the family named by `kind`, fills its parameters from `params` **in the order of [`Kind`](../Kind.md)**, and validates the result (positive volatilities, correlations inside (−1, 1), and so on), so a model that comes back from `make` is always legal. The two signatures differ only in how the numbers are given: a braced list (the usual way) or a `std::span` over existing data. `fin::model::make` is the same function. `cfg` selects the data type and device of the parameter `Series`; the default is Float64.

## Parameters

`model::Kind kind`
: The family.

`std::span<const double> params / std::initializer_list<double>`
: The parameters in the family's order.

`pluss::Config cfg`
: Type and device of the parameter `Series`.

## Returns

A validated `Model`.

## Errors

- A wrong parameter count or a parameter outside its domain throws (`pluss::Error`).

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A Heston model from a braced list.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const mod::Model m = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04});
  out.writeln(m.name(), m.parameters().items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2

From existing data: a `std::vector` as a span. This is how an optimiser's trial vector becomes a model.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <vector>
#include <span>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const std::vector<double> trial = {0.2, 1.0, 0.4, -0.3};
  const mod::Model m = mod::Model::make(fin::model::Kind::Sabr, std::span<const double>(trial.data(), trial.size()));
  out.writeln(m.name(), m.parameters().items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3

Validation on construction. A correlation outside (−1, 1) and a non-positive `kappa` are both refused, together.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <string>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  try {
    (void)(fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {-1.0, 0.04, 0.3, -1.2, 0.04}));
  } catch (const std::exception &e) {
    const std::string text(e.what());
    out.writeln(text.substr(0, text.find("Triggered")));
  }
}
```

### Example 4

The stored type. The parameters of the held struct are Float64 by default; a `Config` chooses the type they are stored in (the vector read back by `parameters()` is Float64 unless asked otherwise).

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const mod::Model a = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2});
  const mod::Model b = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}, pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float32));
  out.writeln("default:", a.as<fin::model::BlackScholes>().volatility.dtype(), ", Float32 config:", b.as<fin::model::BlackScholes>().volatility.dtype());
}
```

### Example 5

A wrong count: the message gives the expected order.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <string>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  try {
    (void)(fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Bates, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}));
  } catch (const std::exception &e) {
    const std::string text(e.what());
    out.writeln(text.substr(0, text.find('\n')));
  }
}
```

